  "title": "SCA friction: a fleet whose 3DS quality is decorrelated from its authorization quality",
  "description": "The world #11's decomposition has to be right in, and the one a 3DS term is wrong in. Two things are deliberate. (1) 3DS quality is DECORRELATED from auth quality: delta is the auth-strongest acquirer (base 0.935) with the second-worst frictionless rate (0.62) and the second-worst challenge abandonment (0.28), while charlie is auth-weak (0.842) and 3DS-strong (0.88 frictionless, 0.19 abandonment). In a fleet where 3DS quality is a proxy for auth quality (spikes/0003-0004's 'correlated' world) a term that confuses them still ranks correctly; here it does not. (2) The funnel is heterogeneous by merchant category, because the ticket says the 10-30% dropout 'varies by merchant vertical': travel and gaming challenge more (mcc multiplier 0.90/0.85 on the frictionless rate, as the grammar allows) and their challenges are abandoned more often. The second effect is a SPIKE-LOCAL model extension: the scenario grammar can express per-category CHALLENGE rates (frictionless_multiplier) but not per-category ABANDONMENT, so the abandonment multipliers live in sca_friction.py as declared constants and are flagged as a missing scenario capability in ADR-0010's payload for #17. Everything else is inherited from baseline-steady-v1 and hashes with it: same fleet, same economics (via the catalog hash), same context mix, same seed.",
